  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "ACT 8: THE NEW BASELINE"
  - line: 148
    type: narration
    text: "The Guild’s healers tended to Kyh."
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "Oreck oversaw the few slaves they’d managed to pull through the door, his presence a steady, protective rock."
  - line: 150
    type: narration
    text: "Kulla sat in a corner, silently repairing his damaged leg with mortar pilfered from a guild wall, grumbling about the poor quality."
  - line: 152
    type: narration
    text: "Geralt stood at a crystalline window, looking out at the Earth, a blue-green gem in the black."
  - line: 154
    type: narration
    text: "The Asteroid Spire was offline."
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "A victory."
  - line: 156
    type: narration
    text: "Kyh had joined the location to the network."
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "A victory."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "They had saved a handful of lives."
  - line: 159
    type: narration
    text: "A victory."
  - line: 161
    type: narration
    text: "But the cost was etched into him."
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "The numbness of the Anchor."
  - line: 163
    type: narration
    text: "The scorched feel of the Applicator in his mind."
  - line: 164
    type: narration
    text: "The sight of hundreds more they couldn’t save."
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "And the certain, chilling knowledge of the Queen’s now-personal attention."
  - line: 167
    type: narration
    text: "This wasn’t an end."
  - line: 168
    type: narration
    text: "It was a pivot."
  - line: 169
    type: narration
    text: "The next phase of Luminaire’s plan was now in motion."
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "The network had its first, hard-won extension."
  - line: 171
    type: narration
    text: "The long, slow work of building a web to cradle a sleeping Earth could begin."
  - line: 173
    type: narration
    text: "And he, Geralt, the Anchor, was now prepared for his part."
  - line: 174
    type: narration
    text: "The generations of solitude."
  - line: 175
    type: narration
    text: "The vigil in the solar cocoon."
  - line: 176
    type: narration
    text: "He had the discipline to endure it."
  - line: 178
    type: narration
    text: "He felt a presence then, not in the room, but in the elements."
  - line: 179
    type: narration
    text: "A whisper in the geothermal vent’s steam, a sigh in the stone, a chime in the floating orbs of light."
  - line: 181
    type: narration
    text: "The Five Mikas."
  - line: 182
    type: narration
    text: "They didn’t speak words."
  - line: 183
    type: narration
    text: "They communicated a feeling."
  - line: 184
    type: narration
    text: "A complex, layered emotion of acknowledgment, of sorrow for the cost, and of unwavering, elemental support."
  - line: 185
    type: narration
    text: "They were with him."
  - line: 186
    type: narration
    text: "They were in the world he was fighting for."
  - line: 187
    type: narration
    text: "Her legacy was alive."
  - line: 189
    type: narration
    text: "He placed his hand against the cool crystal of the window."
  - line: 191
    type: narration
    text: "The quiet war had begun."
  - line: 192
    type: narration
    text: "And he was its first, and most patient, soldier."
  - line: 194
    type: narration
    text: "end of chapter 055-the anchors forge"

